# API Test Template

Purpose:
  Manual API testing instructions for DB → BE → BE_TS → API → API_TS chain.
  Used when the task chain is purely backend (no UI layer yet).

Owns: testing\API-TEST-TEMPLATE.sdd

## Chain Context

Chain: DB → BE → BE_TS → API → API_TS
Mode: Manual API testing via curl

## Test Case Format

Test_Case:
  Hash: #{hash}
  Endpoint: {HTTP_METHOD} {URL}
  Headers:
    - Content-Type: application/json
    - Authorization: Bearer <TEST_TOKEN>
  Body:
    {json_payload}
  Expected_Response:
    {expected_json_or_status}

## Example

Example:
  #c4d1 — Escrow calculation endpoint:
    curl -X POST https://api.edunexusaz.local/v1/payment/escrow \
      -H "Content-Type: application/json" \
      -H "Authorization: Bearer <TEST_TOKEN>" \
      -d '{"completion_pct": 60, "course_price": 100}'

    Expected response:
      {"teacher_payout": 50, "platform_fee": 15, "status": "escrowed"}

## Operator Feedback

Feedback:
  Operator responds per hash:
    #c4d1: OK
    #c4d2: FAIL — wrong payout amount

State: +
